{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1795824452","published":"2026-11-28T00:07:45Z","modified":"2026-11-28T00:58:20.303970001Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-101296","CVE-2026-41293","CVE-2026-76183","CVE-2026-77791","CVE-2026-78383","CVE-2026-79677","CVE-2026-86350"],"summary":"tomcat: Fix of 6 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-86350: validate HTTP/2 request header fields in Stream.emitHeader()\n  instead of in the HPACK decoder, so an invalid field only resets its stream\n  and the HPACK dynamic table stays in sync for later requests on the\n  connection; the decoder-side validation came from the earlier\n  CVE-2026-41293 backport (upstream tomcat 9.0.122)\n- CVE-2026-101296: always use a simple bind to check the password of a user in\n  JNDIRealm, whatever authentication mechanism the realm is configured with\n  (upstream tomcat 9.0.123)\n- CVE-2026-78383: do not wait for an unread AJP request body when the request\n  ended in error, and close the AJP connection after such a request so that\n  the unread body is not read as a new request (upstream tomcat 9.0.122 and an\n  unreleased 9.0.x follow-up)\n- CVE-2026-79677: track WebSocket asynchronous write timeouts in a set that is\n  not ordered by expiry and update it under a lock, so that every write that\n  times out is detected (upstream tomcat 9.0.122)\n- CVE-2026-76183: do not treat braces in a WebSocket request path as URI\n  template parameters when looking for a matching endpoint, which allowed a\n  security constraint bypass (upstream tomcat 9.0.122)\n- CVE-2026-77791: sleep instead of yielding while a WebSocket close message\n  waits for a pending write, so that the waiting thread no longer keeps a CPU\n  busy (upstream tomcat 9.0.122)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"tomcat","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.6","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/tomcat?distro=almalinux-9.6"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:9.0.87-3.el9_6.3.tuxcare.els20"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github